  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Given that $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{2}{3}$ and $\\theta$ is in Quadrant I, find each of the following:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p7-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin 2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{4\\sqrt{5}}{9}$",
          "worked": "Since $\\theta$ is in Quadrant I, $\\sin\\theta>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\theta&=\\sqrt{1-\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^2}\\\\\\sin\\theta&=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\\\\\sin 2\\theta&=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\\\\\sin 2\\theta&=2\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\right)\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)\\\\\\sin 2\\theta&=\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{9}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos 2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\dfrac{1}{9}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos 2\\theta&=2\\cos^2\\theta-1\\\\\\cos 2\\theta&=2\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^2-1\\\\\\cos 2\\theta&=\\frac{8}{9}-1\\\\\\cos 2\\theta&=-\\frac{1}{9}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\tan 2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-4\\sqrt{5}$",
          "worked": "Using $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}$ from part (a):\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}/3}{2/3}\\\\\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\\\\\tan 2\\theta&=\\frac{2\\tan\\theta}{1-\\tan^2\\theta}\\\\\\tan 2\\theta&=\\frac{2(\\sqrt{5}/2)}{1-(\\sqrt{5}/2)^2}\\\\\\tan 2\\theta&=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{-1/4}\\\\\\tan 2\\theta&=-4\\sqrt{5}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      }
    ]
  },
